# Spike workflow

`spikes/sN.yaml` describes the shape of one spike. It is both the contract and the result record. It is not a roadmap of future spikes.

## Gate

- At most one spike has `status: open`.
- Create the next spike only after the previous one is `closed` or `dropped`.
- Each spike lives in `spikes/sN.yaml` (`s1`, `s2`, …) and follows `spike.template.yaml`.
- With no open spike, do not change project files. Exceptions: writing `spikes/sN.yaml` when the user has agreed to open, change, close, or drop that spike; writing `proposed-spikes.yaml` as the proposal set.
- While a spike is `open`, change only paths in `constraints.touches`, plus that spike’s own `spikes/sN.yaml`. Update the spike file as the contract and the result record.

## Contract before work

- `goal.statement` — one outcome in the project.
- `done_when` — checkable criteria (a command or a read).
- `out_of_scope` — required and non-empty before work starts.
- `source.question` — exactly one unknown.

## Tests

- Tests are local and do not call live models, search engines, or clusters.
- A test that needs an external system is a command for the user to run. Do not run it against that system.

## Close or drop

- The user decides whether the spike is `closed` or `dropped`. Do not set either status on your own.
- `closed`: set `documentation.decision` and one `documentation.evidence` entry for each `done_when` item.
- `dropped`: set `documentation.drop_reason`.
- `documentation.leftover` states only what the next spike may start from.

```yaml
# ❌ several later spikes written into this one
goal:
  statement: |
    Outcome A, then outcome B, then outcome C.
leftover:
  - start outcome B
  - start outcome C

# ✅ one outcome; leftover is only a possible start for the next spike
goal:
  statement: |
    <one outcome in the project>
  done_when:
    - "<command or readable check>"
  out_of_scope:
    - "<excluded work>"
source:
  question: |
    <exactly one unknown>
constraints:
  touches:
    - <path this spike may change>
documentation:
  evidence:
    - "<result of the done_when check>"
  leftover:
    - "<fact the next spike may start from>"
```
